{
    "background_story": "Zyon was a curious sea urchin who lived in the vibrant coral reef. As a larva, Zyon underwent a remarkable transformation, his body folding inward to form a blastopore - a opening that would eventually become his mouth. This early developmental stage was crucial in shaping his future as a sea urchin. As he grew, Zyon's blastopore transformed into a sophisticated feeding system, allowing him to capture plankton and small invertebrates with ease. Zyon's unique feature became a topic of fascination among the reef's inhabitants, who would often gather to watch him feed. Despite his unusual appearance, Zyon thrived in the reef, using his blastopore to sustain himself and contribute to the delicate balance of the ecosystem. His story served as a reminder of the incredible diversity and adaptability of life in the ocean.",
